Phase 2 implementation and verification (2026-10-16)
  Repository baseline: 84d51a1e. Installed VSEssentials.dll SHA256 remains the Phase 1 value above.
  Source paths below are relative to VanillaGraphicsExpanded/; test names resolve in the test project.

  Task-to-document and implementation traceability
    - Native adapters -> Proposal / Ownership boundary, Simple cloud rendering, Publication and native
      lifecycle; Phase 1 / Native producer and Borrowed input contracts -> PBR/Clouds/CloudNativeMapAdapter,
      CloudMapPublication and CloudNativeSimpleAdapter, with three map producer hooks (generation,
      upload and allocation) and a separate CloudVolumetricDrawHook ownership gate.
      Certificates require supported storage/attachments/formats, linked program, an observed
      successful joint raw upload and successful current-frame generation. Rebuilds invalidate before
      deletion, including reused names. Reload/failure/teardown withdraw publication. Placement is copied
      after generation; mesh access occurs after native tick or within a paused callback and ends at
      submission. The Simple adapter performs update, capture and synchronous submission in one method;
      no Simple tick/rebuild/reload observer or persistent mesh-borrow tracker is installed. Its actual
      replacement callback is added with the functioning shader in Phase 3. Native owners retain their
      shader subscriptions, fields and disposal authority.
    - Lifecycle/resources -> Proposal / Publication and native lifecycle; Atmosphere.Publication / Ownership
      and Publication contract; BaselineShading / Scope and shared contracts -> ModSystems/CloudModSystem,
      PBR/Clouds/CloudNativeRuntime and CloudModeOwnership. Existing context registry, shader-reload admission
      and cleanup owners supply lifecycle boundaries. World epochs/root matching reject obsolete owners.
      VgeFrameRenderer.TryGetCurrentFrame allows unavailable camera inputs to be omitted without throwing
      through native draws. No atmospheric publication, native compatibility allowance or user setting changes.
      Ownership admission requires the selected functioning draw; the volume callback gate reconciles
      the live preference at draw time and release disposes only accepted VGE resources. Native settings
      watchers keep their registration authority; VGE performs no volume register/unregister operations.
      No draw consumer is installed yet, so native drawing remains active. Dedicated shader declarations/build registration
      accompany their actual Simple/Volumetric programs in Phases 3–4; GPU targets/history belong to their
      later owners. No placeholder executable, duplicate shader registry or per-frame GPU allocation is added.
    - Deterministic verification -> Proposal / Acceptance and implementation qualification and the Phase 2
      test requirements -> CloudMapPublicationTests, CloudModeOwnershipTests,
      CloudNativeSimpleAdapterTests, CloudNativeHookTests and GPU/CloudNativeAdapterTests. Cover uninitialized
      allocation, failed in-place upload/generation, skipped native bodies, changed dimensions/handles,
      same-name rebuild, reload failure/recovery, pause/current placement, disposed/uninitialized meshes,
      missing camera, foreign/old-world roots, world-teardown invalidation, draw suppression/restoration
      without registration changes and disposal ownership.
      Three map observer hooks install against native methods and have no suppressing prefixes;
      the volume draw gate permits native drawing until a functioning consumer owns the selected mode. Tiny
      headless GL fixtures exercise link/storage/error checks and restore separate read/draw FBO bindings.

